[I] A web browser built on the LibWeb and LibJS engines

[T] Ladybird is a web browser built on the LibWeb and LibJS engines.
[T] The Browser UI has a cross-platform GUI in Qt6 and a macOS-specific GUI in AppKit.

[U] https://github.com/LadybirdBrowser/ladybird

[A] SerenityOS Devs
[M] René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>

[C] extra/office
[F] CROSS NO-LTO OBJDIR

[E] opt libjxl
[E] add liberation-fonts
[E] opt libwebp

[L] BSD
[V] 2026.47.7

[D] 4a633977f379c204f456d556e6a7a4aceae6bd1c6791a79095c7ae3e ladybird-2026.47.7.tar.zst git+https://github.com/LadybirdBrowser/ladybird 2026.47.7

var_append GCC_WRAPPER_APPEND ' ' "-L`pkgprefix libdir libwebp`"
pkginstalled qt6base || var_append cmakeopt ' ' -DENABLE_QT=OFF
var_append cmakeopt ' ' "-GNinja -DBUILD_TESTING=OFF -DLADYBIRD_ENABLE_CCACHE=OFF"
var_append cmakeopt ' ' "-Dunofficial-angle_DIR=$root/$(pkgprefix angle)/share/unofficial-angle"
# TODO: this is a hack for minimum O2, fails inlining w/ less
var_append GCC_WRAPPER_APPEND ' ' '*Normalize.cpp*?-O2'
var_append GCC_WRAPPER_APPEND ' ' "-I$root/$(pkgprefix includedir skia)"

atstage cross && var_append cmakeopt ' ' -DLAGOM_USE_LINKER=bfd
